  "userdoc": {
   "kind": "user",
   "methods": {
    "cancelUpgrade()": {
     "notice": "\u00a7N2 - cancel the queued upgrade (admin only). "
    },
    "changeProxyAdmin(address)": {
     "notice": "Rotate the proxy admin (e.g., move from deployer EOA -> multisig). "
    },
    "pendingUpgrade()": {
     "notice": "\u00a7N2 - views for monitoring/queued-upgrade transparency. "
    },
    "proposeUpgrade(address,bytes)": {
     "notice": "\u00a7Code-Review N2 - step 1 of the two-step upgrade: queue the new implementation (and the exact migration calldata, committed by hash). Only the proxy admin may propose. The queued upgrade becomes executable via `upgradeToAndCall` after UPGRADE_TIMELOCK elapses. Proposing again overwrites the previous proposal (restarting the clock), so a mis-queued upgrade is corrected by re-proposing."
    },
    "upgradeToAndCall(address,bytes)": {
     "notice": "Step 2 of the two-step upgrade: swap the implementation. Only the proxy admin may execute, ONLY for the exact (implementation, data) pair queued via `proposeUpgrade`, and ONLY after the proxy-layer timelock has elapsed (\u00a7Code-Review N2 - identity AND process). Optionally re-runs an init/migration call on the new implementation in the same tx."
    }
   },
   "notice": "EIP-1967 minimal UUPS proxy used as the M3 upgrade scaffold. Why a custom proxy rather than OZ's `UUPSUpgradeable`? - We already lean on a hand-rolled GilderAccessControl for role   management; pulling in OpenZeppelin's full Initializable + UUPS   stack would force every M1/M2 contract to be refactored to   `initializer` modifier semantics and constructorless storage. This   proxy keeps the existing `initialize(...)` pattern, just behind a   delegatecall layer. New M3+ modules can opt in. Upgrade flow:   1. Deploy a fresh implementation contract.   2. Call `upgradeTo(newImpl)` on the proxy. Only DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE      may upgrade (gated by the implementation's access control,      because the role check happens in the delegated `_authorizeUpgrade`).   3. Implementation storage layout MUST be append-only - that's why      every Gilder module already reserves a `uint256[N] __gap`. Storage layout uses the EIP-1967 standard slots so an off-chain indexer (or a block explorer's \"Read as Proxy\" view) can resolve the implementation address without a special getter.",
   "version": 1
  }
 },
